::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-shelf-render, dependencies: list(tomet-shelf-config, tomet-shelf-document, tomet-shelf-icons), dependents: list(tomet-shelf-headless, tomet-shelf-template)}

=[tomet-shelf-render]

HTML tag injection and presentation rendering for `tomet-shelf`.

Provides post-processing and HTML tag injection for document markup:

- Code block decoration (language badge, copy button)
- List marker enhancement (task checkboxes, badge pills)
- Link icon enhancement (external brand/favicons, internal note icons)
- `@doc.icon` custom element rendering
- HTML escaping and presentation formatters

==[Module code]

Code block enhancement: wraps `<pre><code>` blocks with a header bar containing
an optional language label (top-left) and a clipboard copy button (top-right).

===[Functions]

====[fn enhance_code_blocks]

Enhances code blocks in the rendered HTML by wrapping them in a container
with a language label and a copy button.

==[Module doc_icon]

Renders `@doc.icon("name", pkg:"lucide")` via a pluggable [`IconRenderer`].

Tomet resolves this element but deliberately never draws it, by design: an
external renderer is meant to implement the notation. This module connects
the element to [`IconRenderer`] (wired in as a
`tomet_html::RenderOptions::custom_element` hook).

If no [`IconRenderer`] is configured or an unknown icon is requested,
a visible placeholder is rendered so typos in documents are visible.

===[Functions]

====[fn render_doc_icon]

Renders a `@doc.icon` custom element into HTML.

====[fn create_doc_icon_custom_element]

Creates a `CustomElementRenderer` that handles `@doc.icon` elements.

==[Module external_links]

External link enhancement: adds brand SVG icons (via Simple Icons) or
dynamic favicons (via Google Favicon API or DuckDuckGo) to external links.

===[Functions]

====[fn enhance_external_links]

Enhances external links in rendered HTML by inserting a site/brand icon prefix.

==[Module html]

Building blocks for the HTML this crate assembles by hand.

Infobox values reach the template through `| safe`, so anything produced
here has to be safe to drop straight into the page.

===[Functions]

====[fn escape_html]

Escape text for interpolation into HTML text nodes and double-quoted attributes.

====[fn sanitize_color_hex]

Normalize a `@meta.colors` entry to a bare hex body (`#AABBCC` -> `aabbcc`).

Returns `None` for anything that is not a 3/4/6/8-digit hex color, which keeps
unvetted text out of the inline `style` attributes that consume it.

====[fn color_chip_html]

A colour swatch, or plain escaped text when the value is not a hex colour.

====[fn external_link_html]

====[fn is_external_url]

==[Module internal_links]

Internal link enhancement: adds note icon prefixes (from note's @meta.icon)
to internal links matching published documents in the vault.

===[Functions]

====[fn enhance_internal_links]

Enhances internal links in rendered HTML by inserting the target note's icon prefix.

==[Module marker]

List marker processing: enhances `tomet-html`'s `<span class="tm-list-marker">`
into Lucide SVG icons (for checkboxes and task markers) or clean badge pills (for
timestamps, tags, and unmapped text).

===[Functions]

====[fn enhance_list_markers]

Enhances list markers in the rendered HTML:

- Replaces checkbox/icon markers with Lucide SVGs (if `config.enable` is true)
- Replaces raw bracketed text markers `[xxx]` with pill badges
- Injects task item classes onto enclosing `<li>`s

==[Module meta]

===[Functions]

====[fn format_text_icon]

Formats a plain text or emoji icon string according to avatar display rules:

- 1 char -- single large glyph (`avatar-text-1`)
- 2 chars -- horizontally auto-scaled without wrapping (`avatar-text-2`)
- 3 chars -- 2x2 grid with 3rd item centered on bottom row (`avatar-grid avatar-grid-3`)
- 4 chars -- 2x2 grid (`avatar-grid avatar-grid-4`)
- 5 or more chars -- initials (first 2 graphemes rendered with `avatar-text-2 avatar-initials`)

====[fn format_text_icon_link]

====[fn render_page_icon]

Renders a structured `DocIcon` into an HTML representation for page headers/chrome.

====[fn render_page_link_icon]

Renders a structured `DocIcon` into a small link prefix HTML icon.

==[Functions]

===[fn enhance_body_html]

Enhances a raw HTML body string by injecting presentation tags:
list markers, code blocks, and external links.
